  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8a3676f4eac94dd6881061ea0f360c41",
      "statement": "src/shared/feature.ts defines the Feature contract (name plus optional start/stop/addToWindow/removeFromWindow; stop and removeFromWindow synchronous). Its helpers startAll and addToWindow invoke the hook for every feature in array order, collect async hooks' promises and await them all; stopAll and removeFromWindow walk the array in reverse order so teardown unwinds startup. Every hook runs through one invoke() wrapper that catches sync throws and converts async rejections into log calls, so a failing feature never aborts the others and none of the four helpers ever throws or rejects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/shared/feature.ts#L7-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b43a9a65c6255f6db1e2888bb359657c3b0aaaf55e4ede8fecdb91cb7db3afd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://test-unit/feature.test.ts#L14-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83033d9d9e590b7e7e284450d34d2ccd45185fd6a20f4fdef3b0c6905093e6ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23e4632130d8443c9a841132be80d6ad",
      "statement": "The registry's defaultLogger resolves the ztoolkit global lazily at call time and wraps both ztoolkit.log and Zotero.logError in try/catch, so logging a failed hook never disturbs the caller and src/shared/feature.ts stays importable in Node without any Zotero globals (pinned by test-unit/feature.test.ts).",
      "evidence": [
